// Package schema generates the JSON Schemas (draft 2020-12) of the agent-facing contracts from the domain types, so
// an agent's tool schema cannot drift from the code that validates it.
//
// # Purpose
//
// Each registered id (FindingIn@1, Review@1, TaskEnvelope@1, TestSubmission@1, Verdict@1) names one contract. The
// schema is generated by reflection over the domain struct, with the jsonschema struct tags as the only source of
// limits, enums and descriptions. This package is an adapter: it may import domain packages and nothing else internal.
//
// # API
//
//   - IDs returns the registered ids in order.
//   - Schema(id) returns the indented, newline-terminated schema of one id, or an error naming the registered ids.
//     The output is deterministic, so testdata/<id>.schema.json is compared byte for byte.
//
// # Invariants
//
//   - Every limit in a schema (minLength, maxLength, minItems, maxItems) equals the Go constant it mirrors. The tests
//     derive the expected values from the constants, so a changed constant without a changed tag fails.
//   - Every enum equals the set its Parse function accepts, and the golden examples in the domain testdata use only
//     declared properties and listed enum values.
//   - Generation does not reference definitions; each schema is self-contained.
//
// # What the schema cannot say
//
// The generated schemas are structural. These rules are enforced only by the Go Validate methods, not by the schema:
//
//   - the line order (first at most last) and the 1-based lines;
//   - the clean-path rule of file names (no "..", no absolute path, no backslash);
//   - the per-kind form of a citation ref (run id, finding name);
//   - the form of acceptance-criteria keys (AC2), and the case id pattern is in the schema but the Go check is authoritative;
//   - the character counts after trimming (the schema counts raw characters, so a claim of padded spaces passes the
//     schema and fails Validate);
//   - the TaskEnvelope carries no jsonschema tags, because it is defined in the workflow package, so its schema has
//     types and required fields only.
//
// # Failure modes
//
//   - An unknown id is an error, never an empty schema.
//   - Validation of an example against a real JSON Schema validator is NOT verified: no validator is in go.sum and
//     none was added. The tests check the structure instead (declared keys, required keys, enum values, limits).
//
// # Tests
//
//   - schema_test.go: the registered ids, the golden match of every schema, determinism over repeated runs, the
//     draft and object shape, every limit against its constant, required fields, enum sets against the parsers' values
//     and the golden examples' keys and enum values.
//
// Layout and dependency rule: docs/TECH_SPEC.md section 2.2, enforced by internal/archcheck.
package schema
